				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireintheseeyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6074764); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6074764&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609250027" alt="FireInTheseEyes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6074764)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireintheseeyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6074764); return false;" >FireInTheseEyes</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609249604 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Dec 2020 13:46</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13964402/seeking-greenlight-the-object">Seeking Greenlight - The &quot;Object&quot;</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4856602">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> I do not have a complete page layout yet, however I would add in logs and addenda of stories and experiments involving encounters with this SCP in the main article.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-xxxx is an invisible object that cannot be detected by any kind of conventional scanning ray. Once at a location, it seeks out groups of 2+ individuals engaged in conversation. It will then proceed to take the form of whatever it is the speakers are presently discussing, including living creatures. When transformed into another object/being, the SCP will behave in a fashion consistent with the speakers' perception of the object/being. If uninterrupted by another transformation, the SCP's current transformation will last one hour before it goes back to its invisible state.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-xxxx was found in a hospital in 198x, following originally incredulous reports from the hospital's psychiatric ward. By the time it was captured by the SCP foundation it had indirectly caused 3 casualties and directly caused 1 casualty. Descriptions of the way the casualties came to be will be included. Witnesses at the hospital have been administered Class C amnestics.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> While there are other SCPs with the ability to transform (for example, SCP-2006), the &quot;object&quot; does not have a particular reason for doing so. It is &quot;benign&quot;, because it does not seek to cause harm unless the speakers are discussing something dangerous. This way, there also is the possibility that a group of people could control it and gain great power; for example, the SCP could be helpful if it is made to transform into a tool or other instrument, but it could become scary if it is made to transform into a living murderer with a knife.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I am thinking that perhaps the narrative should focus more on the breadth of incidents that can be caused by this anomaly rather than the casualties per se.</p>

							</div>

								
					
