<blockquote>
<p>then recounting an exact replica of the events that occurred at the PCS facility, except it's an interview recounting the exact same events occurring at a SCP facility.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For a second, I thought this was going to lead into the discovery that the two organisations are the same and that there's some kinda anomaly that means some foundation sites aren't recognised as such or w/e.</p>
<p>I think at the end of the day, my core issue with this as a concept can be summarised as 'so what?': the impact of discovering the PCS Foundation, and the question of whether they're actually real, feels very minimal because I'm not really sure what it changes in like, my understanding of what's going on here? Like it feels like it's meant to have a big shocking moment where we realise 'oh! second foundation!' but there's no exploration of the implications of it's existence.</p>
<p>I'm also not necessarily convinced by this as a SCP article: what's the like, description/conprocs about? The PCS foundation? If so, the choice to have the two identical incidents happens feels even weirder because what do they actually like, add to the narrative here beyond reiterating what we already know?</p>
